eptance Criteria, HLR Traceability. For E001 (Investigation) also questions/deliverable. Add relevant extra sections: for E001, \"Questions to resolve\". \n\nLet me draft each epic body.\n\nE001 body:\n\n# Legal clearance for redistributing an AGPL-3.0 S3-compatible object store\n\n## Description\nResolves whether MinIO (AGPL-3.0) can be redistributed as a bundled, supported component of the platform, including the derivative-work posture for operator integration, and documents the decision. If the terms cannot be satisfied, the investigation confirms the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate (e.g., SeaweedFS) and records that the image productization work must restart against the new upstream.\n\n## Scope\n- Legal review of redistributing MinIO under AGPL-3.0 in the product distribution model\n- Derivative-work posture for integrating the store with the Platform Operator (aggregation vs. derivative work)\n- Documented clearance decision, including any conditions imposed\n- Confirmation of the fallback candidate and restart impact if clearance is denied\n\n## Questions to Resolve\n1. Can MinIO (AGPL-3.0) be redistributed in our disconnected-install distribution model?\n2. Does operator integration (bundling, lifecycle management) create a derivative work under AGPL-3.0, and if so, can the posture be made acceptable?\n3. If not cleared: is the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate (e.g., SeaweedFS) confirmed as the replacement upstream?\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Given the legal review of AGPL-3.0 redistribution terms, When the review completes, Then the clearance decision (including derivative-work posture for operator integration) is documented, and either redistribution is cleared or the fallback upstream is confirmed with the restart of image productization planned.\n- Measured by: a written clearance decision accessible to all downstream teams; downstream scoping epics unblocked.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-1 (P0): legal review completed and documented.\n\nHmm, the AC format \"Given/When/Then with measured by\" — the strategy has no ACs, so I derive them. Fine.\n\nE002 body (repo-onboarding):\n\n# Midstream repo onboarding for the bundled object store\n\n## Description\nCreates the midstream repository for the legally cleared S3-compatible object store candidate under opendatahub-io, establishing the fork point, branch strategy, and build packaging scaffolding needed to productize the store's container image.\n\n## Scope\n- Midstream fork/repo creation for the cleared object store candidate under opendatahub-io\n- Initial import of the selected upstream release\n- Repo configuration (CI triggers, OWNERS, README) consistent with other midstream component repos\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Given the clearance decision, When the midstream repository is created, Then it contains the cleared candidate's source at the selected upstream release and follows opendatahub-io midstream repo conventions.\n- The repo is ready for build-pipeline onboarding (no pipeline configuration in this epic).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-2 (P0): productized images for the bundled store (repo foundation).\n\nE003 (license-validation):\n\n# License validation for the bundled object store\n\n## Description\nRuns license scanning over the cleared object store candidate and its transitive dependencies to produce the license bill of materials for the productized image, surfacing any copyleft or otherwise problematic transitive dependencies beyond the headline AGPL question.\n\n## Scope\n- License scan of the candidate's source and dependency tree\n- Report of transitive dependency licenses and any findings\n- Escalation of findings that conflict with the redistribution posture\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Given the cleared candidate, When license scanning completes, Then a license report covering the full transitive dependency tree of the productized image is produced and any blocking findings are escalated before implementation work proceeds.\n- Measured by: scan report attached to the epic; no unresolved blocking license findings.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-1/HLR-2 (P0): documents the licensing posture of the redistributed store and its dependencies.\n\nE004 (konflux-onboarding):\n\n# Konflux onboarding for the object store build pipeline\n\n## Description\nOnboards the object store midstream repository to Konflux so its container image is built and released through the standard product build pipeline.\n\n## Scope\n- Konflux application and component configuration for the object store repo\n- Image build recipe and release pipeline configuration\n- Verification that a green build of the store image completes through Konflux\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Given the midstream repository exists, When Konflux onboarding completes, Then the object store image builds green through the standard pipeline.\n- Measured by: successful Konflux build of the store image.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-2 (P0): productized images with a supported build lifecycle.\n\nE005 (general implementation, operator enablement):\n\n# Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store\n\n## Description\nDelivers administrator-facing enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store through the Platform Operator: deploying the productized store image with the platform's upgrade lifecycle, so disconnected and PoC clusters can run a supported store instead of ad hoc upstream installs.\n\n## Scope\n- Operator-managed deployment of the productized object store image\n- Administrator enablement controls (opt-in for disconnected/PoC clusters)\n- Upgrade lifecycle integration (image updates flow through the operator's upgrade path)\n- Upgrade/rollback behavior for the enabled store (admin can disable without data loss? hmm — careful not to invent) \n\nCareful — scope constraint: don't invent CRD fields. Keep capability level:\n- Operator-managed deployment and lifecycle of the bundled store\n- Administrator opt-in enablement\n- Upgrade lifecycle integration\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Given the bundled store image and its midstream repo, When an administrator enables the store through the Platform Operator, Then a supported S3-compatible object store runs on the cluster and is managed through the platform upgrade lifecycle.\n- The store's build pipeline is green (Konflux-built image).\n- Enabling/disabling the store does not affect customer-provided S3 configurations (out of scope remains out).\n- Measured by: admin can enable and use the store on a disconnected cluster without manual upstream installation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-2 (P0): administrators can enable a supported, bundled store through the Platform Operator with productized images and upgrade lifecycle.\n\nE006 (DSP defaults):\n\n# Data Science Pipelines defaults for the bundled store\n\n## Description\nUpdates Data Science Pipelines so that artifact storage connection defaults target the bundled S3-compatible store on clusters where it is enabled, without manual endpoint configuration.\n\n## Scope\n- Default artifact storage connection targeting the bundled store when enabled\n- No manual endpoint configuration required when the bundled store is present\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Given a cluster with the bundled store enabled, When a user creates a Data Science Pipelines application, Then its artifact storage defaults to the bundled store with no manual endpoint configuration.\n- Clusters using customer-provided S3 continue to work unchanged.\n- Measured by: pipeline runs store artifacts in the bundled store with zero-config on a disconnected cluster.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-3 (P1): DSP connection defaults target the bundled store.\n\nE007 (Dashboard defaults):\n\n# Dashboard model serving connection defaults for the bundled store\n\n## Description\nUpdates the Dashboard so that model serving data connection defaults target the bundled S3-compatible store on clusters where it is enabled, removing manual endpoint configuration for serving workloads.\n\n## Scope\n- Model serving connection defaults in the Dashboard targeting the bundled store when enabled\n- Existing user-created connections continue to take precedence (hmm — inventing policy? \"can target the bundled store without manual endpoint configuration\" — defaults imply user config overrides. I'll phrase: explicit user-configured connections continue to be honored.)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Given a cluster with the bundled store enabled, When a user configures model serving through the Dashboard, Then connection defaults target the bundled store with no manual endpoint configuration.\n- Measured by: serving deployment using the bundled store with zero-config on a disconnected cluster.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-3 (P1): model serving connection defaults target the bundled store.\n\nE008 (docs):\n\n# Documentation for the bundled object store\n\n## Description\nAuthors product documentation for the bundled S3-compatible object store: enablement instructions, sizing guidance, and the supported/unsupported boundary versus customer-provided storage.\n\n## Scope\n- Enablement documentation (admin how-to)\n- Sizing guidance for disconnected/PoC deployments\n- Supported vs. unsupported boundary relative to customer-provided S3 storage\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Documentation covers enablement, sizing guidance, and the supported/unsupported boundary versus customer-provided storage.\n- Technically reviewed against the implemented capability (reviewed by the implementing teams).\n- Measured by: published docs topics covering all HLR-4 areas.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-4 (P2): documentation coverage.\n\nContent outline — the triage docs-only path requires content outline, but this isn't docs-only triage; still, a brief outline is good (Step 8b allows extra sections).\n\nNow signal files. One per epic: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001-ai-signals.md etc.\n\nE001 signals table (investigation):\n| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n| question_specificity | 1 | Concrete, enumerable questions (AGPL redistribution clearance, derivative-work posture for operator integration, fallback confirmation) with a defined pass/fail outcome |\n| source_accessibility | 0 | The answer is a pending legal determination; license texts are readable but the clearance decision does not yet exist in any readable artifact |\n| local_runnability | 0 | Not a component-execution question; no binary/library to exercise for a legal determination |\n| cluster_hardware_dependence | 0 | No cluster or hardware dependence |\n| human_judgment_required | -2 | The gating question is itself a legal/governance decision the AI cannot make |\n\nOK. Now frontmatter sets. Let me be careful with quoting in bash for fallback_approach text.\n\nAlso: dependencies format: \"RHAISTRAT-9012-E001,RHAISTRAT-9012-E002\".\n\nE005 deps: E001,E002,E003.\nE008 deps: E002,E003,E004,E005,E006,E007.\n\ngated_by + gate_failure_impact on E002-E005 (all with gated_by=E001):\n- E002: rewrite, \"If AGPL terms cannot be satisfied, the midstream repo is created for the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate (e.g. SeaweedFS) instead, restarting image productization.\"\n- E003: rewrite, \"If the fallback upstream is selected, the license scan targets the replacement candidate's dependency tree.\"\n- E004: rewrite, \"If the fallback upstream is selected, Konflux onboarding is redone for the replacement repo and image.\"\n- E005: rewrite, \"If the fallback upstream is selected, operator enablement is reimplemented against the replacement store's image and configuration surface.\"\n\nShould E006/E007/E008 have gate_failure_impact? They're gated transitively but their work doesn't change with the outcome (they target \"the bundled store\" regardless). No gated_by. OK.\n\nNow, priorities: E001-E005 P0, E006/E007 P1, E008 P1 (docs exception, Major→P1).\n\nLet me write the files now. First the decomposition summary, then epics, then signals, then frontmatter, then batch-read, then decompose_complete.\n\nLet me check how `frontmatter.py set` handles the decomposition file — does it need a schema? Just run it; if it errors, adapt.\n\nWriting files — I'll do several Write calls in parallel blocks.","signature":"5e6b721fab5b4550ad13dc5f3f4a0c39"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":27132,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af06d9472b104ca0","agent_id":"acaf9d9f56a8e19b4","session_id":"73da6f79-aa1d-41ce-bbe1-bfcaf3dba97b","uuid":"989a60a0-6048-4136-b86e-ababe3bf1ded","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:47:22.978Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9012"}
