{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abb3f05dc486cc47","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: # Legal clearance for redistributing an AGPL-3.0 S3-compatible object store\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: ## Description\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: Resolves whether MinIO (AGPL-3.0) can be redistributed as a bundled, supported\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: component of the platform — including the derivative-work posture for operator\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: integration — and documents the decision. If the terms cannot be satisfied for\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: our distribution model, the investigation confirms the Apache-2.0 fallback\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: candidate (e.g. SeaweedFS) as the replacement upstream and records that image\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: productization work must restart against it. This clearance blocks all\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: shipping work in the strategy.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: ## Scope\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: - Legal review of redistributing MinIO under AGPL-3.0 in the product's\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   distribution model (including disconnected/install-media redistribution)\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: - Determination of the derivative-work posture for integrating the store with\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   the Platform Operator (bundling, deploy, and lifecycle management)\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: - A documented clearance decision, including any conditions imposed\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: - If clearance is denied: confirmation of the fallback candidate and a\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   statement of the restart impact on image productization\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: ## Questions to Resolve\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: 1. Can MinIO (AGPL-3.0) be redistributed in our distribution model for\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:    disconnected installs?\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: 2. Does Platform Operator integration (bundling, deployment, upgrade\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:    management) create a derivative work under AGPL-3.0, and if so, can the\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:    posture be made acceptable?\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: 3. If the terms cannot be satisfied: is the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:    (e.g. SeaweedFS) confirmed as the replacement upstream?\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: ## Acceptance Criteria\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: - Given the legal review of AGPL-3.0 redistribution terms, When the review\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   completes, Then the clearance decision — including the derivative-work\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   posture for operator integration — is documented and accessible to all\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   downstream teams.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: - Measured by: a written clearance decision exists; either redistribution is\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   cleared (possibly with conditions) or the fallback upstream is confirmed\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   with the restart of image productization planned.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: ## HLR Traceability\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md: - HLR-1 (P0): Legal review of redistributing the candidate object store\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   (MinIO, AGPL-3.0) completed and documented, including the derivative-work\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md:   posture for operator integration.\nBODY-REF in artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E001.md\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: # Midstream repo onboarding for the bundled object store\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: ## Description\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: Creates the midstream repository for the legally cleared S3-compatible object\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: store candidate under opendatahub-io, establishing the fork point and repo\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: conventions needed to productize the store's container image. This replaces\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: the current unsupported field practice of installing upstream MinIO ad hoc.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: ## Scope\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: - Midstream repository creation for the cleared object store candidate under\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md:   opendatahub-io\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: - Initial import of the selected upstream release\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: - Repo configuration consistent with other opendatahub-io midstream component\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md:   repos (branch conventions, maintainers, README)\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9012-E002.md: \nartifacts/ep