{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a468b200de8e8a38","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n3\tepic_count: 8\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9012\n11\t\n12\tBundle an S3-compatible object store for disconnected installs.\n13\t\n14\t## Triage\n15\t\n16\tNot below-threshold: the strategy spans multiple components and teams (Platform\n17\tOperator, Data Science Pipelines, Dashboard, Documentation), and contains a\n18\tgenuine P0 unknown (AGPL-3.0 redistribution clearance) whose answer gates all\n19\tshipping work. Not docs-only: code changes are required in the Platform\n20\tOperator, Data Science Pipelines, and Dashboard.\n21\t\n22\t## Epic List\n23\t\n24\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n25\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 | Legal clearance for redistributing an AGPL-3.0 S3-compatible object store | Investigation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E002 | Midstream repo onboarding for the bundled object store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E003 | License validation for the bundled object store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E004 | Konflux onboarding for the object store build pipeline | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 | Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E006 | Data Science Pipelines connection defaults for the bundled store | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P1 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E007 | Dashboard model serving connection defaults for the bundled store | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E008 | Documentation for the bundled object store | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n34\t\n35\tImplementation types: E002 `repo-onboarding`, E003 `license-validation`,\n36\tE004 `konflux-onboarding`, E008 `docs-authoring`; E005-E007 general.\n37\t\n38\t## Dependency DAG\n39\t\n40\t```mermaid\n41\tgraph TD\n42\t    E001[E001 Legal clearance] --> E002[E002 Repo onboarding]\n43\t    E001 --> E003[E003 License validation]\n44\t    E001 --> E004[E004 Konflux onboarding]\n45\t    E001 --> E005[E005 Operator enablement]\n46\t    E002 --> E004\n47\t    E002 --> E005\n48\t    E003 --> E005\n49\t    E005 --> E006[E006 DSP defaults]\n50\t    E005 --> E007[E007 Dashboard defaults]\n51\t    E002 --> E008[E008 Documentation]\n52\t    E003 --> E008\n53\t    E004 --> E008\n54\t    E005 --> E008\n55\t    E006 --> E008\n56\t    E007 --> E008\n57\t```\n58\t\n59\tNote: there is deliberately **no** edge between E004 (Konflux onboarding) and\n60\tE005 (operator enablement) — they run in parallel; the coupling is enforced by\n61\tE005's \"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion, not a DAG dependency.\n62\t\n63\t## DAG Justification\n64\t\n65\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n66\t|------|------|-----------|\n67\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 | Legal clearance (HLR-1) blocks all shipping work; the repo targets the cleared candidate. Gate type: `rewrite` (fallback candidate restarts image productization). |\n68\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 | The license scan target depends on which candidate is cleared. Gate type: `rewrite`. |\n69\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 | Explicit gate edge (transitive via E002): onboarding is redone if the fallback upstream is selected. Gate type: `rewrite`. |\n70\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 | Explicit gate edge (transitive via E002/E003): enablement is reimplemented against the replacement store. Gate type: `rewrite`. |\n71\t| E002 ∥ E003 | Rule 7 | repo-onboarding and license-validation have independent inputs; parallel start. |\n72\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 5 | Konflux onboarding needs the repo; always serial. |\n73\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 6 | General implementation of the onboarded component needs the repo. |\n74\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 9 | If license scanning fails, dependencies change and the approach is affected; serial. |\n75\t| (none) E004 ↔ E005 | Rule 10 | Konflux onboarding is parallel to general implementation; \"build pipeline green\" is an AC on E005, never a DAG edge. |\n76\t| E005 → E006 | Rules 12/13 | DSP connection defaults build against the bundled store capability delivered by the operator. |\n77\t| E005 → E007 | Rules 12/13 | Dashboard model serving connection defaults build against the bundled store capability. |\n78\t| E006 ∥ E007 | Rule 14 | Different repos/components, no shared artifacts; parallel. |\n79\t| E002..E007 → E008 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by all Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. |\n80\t\n81\t## Conditional decomposition decision\n82\t\n83\tThe gating Investigation (E001) has two bounded outcomes: (A) MinIO AGPL-3.0\n84\tclearance granted, (B) fallback to an Apache-2.0 alternative (e.g. SeaweedFS).\n85\tBoth outcomes yield the **same epic structure** — the same onboarding chain,\n86\toperator enablement, consumer defaults, and docs — only the target upstream of\n87\tthe image productization work changes. Because no downstream epic is added or\n88\tremoved by the outcome, no `-BRANCH-` files were created; instead E002-E005\n89\tcarry `gated_by=E001` with `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` describing the\n90\trestart of image productization against the fallback candidate. E006-E008 are\n91\tnot gated: they target \"the bundled store\" identically under either outcome.\n92\t\n93\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n94\t\n95\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epics |\n96\t|-----|----------|-------------|-------|\n97\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Legal review of redistributing the candidate store (MinIO, AGPL-3.0), including derivative-work posture | E001 (decision), E003 (transitive dependency license evidence) |\n98\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible store via the Platform Operator with productized images and upgrade lifecycle | E002, E003, E004, E005 |\n99\t| HLR-3 | P1 | DSP and model serving connection defaults target the bundled store without manual endpoint configuration | E006 (DSP), E007 (model serving via Dashboard) |\n100\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers enablement, sizing guidance, and the supported/unsupported boundary | E008 |\n101\t\n102\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n103\t\n104\t## Component Mappings\n105\t\n106\t- The bundled object store (MinIO or fallback) is a **new component** — it has\n107\t  no entry in `.context/rhai-components.txt` and no architecture context file.\n108\t  Per the component-name constraint, its epics (E002-E004, and the enablement\n109\t  epic E005) use the closest parent-level canonical component, **Platform\n110\t  Operator**, which is the bundling and enablement vehicle. Logged here as a\n111\t  non-obvious mapping.\n112\t- New-component detection triggered Rule 20: full onboarding chain\n113\t  (repo-onboarding + license-validation parallel → konflux-onboarding → general\n114\t  implementation).\n115\t\n116\t## Health Warnings\n117\t\n118\t1. **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n119\t   owner-team column on Affected Components, no Dependencies table, no\n120\t   Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements.\n121\t   Decomposition proceeded from the HLRs and Affected Components list.\n122\t2. **Team assignments are inferred**: \"RHOAI Pipelines\" and \"RHOAI Dashboard\"\n123\t   come from the architecture context owning-team fields; \"RHOAI Platform\n124\t   Operator\" and \"RHOAI Documentation\" are assumed by the same naming\n125\t   convention. Verify with the strategy author.\n126\t3. **Ambiguous component for HLR-3**: the HLR names \"model serving\" connection\n127\t   defaults, but the Affected Components list contains Dashboard (no serving\n128\t   runtime component). The work was mapped to the Dashboard (data connection /\n129\t   serving configuration surface); if the intent was Serving Runtimes or KServe\n130\t   code changes, E007's component assignment should be corrected.\n131\t4. **Priority note (not an inversion)**: E008 is P1 despite covering P2 HLR-4,\n132\t   via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority:\n133\t   Major → P1). It does not push priority upstream to E002-E007.\n134\t5. **Scope watch**: HLR-4's \"sizing guidance\" implies performance\n135\t   characterization of the bundled store that no epic explicitly delivers;\n136\t   sizing content will need input from implementation results (captured as an\n137\t   AC on E008 rather than a new epic, since it is documentation content, not\n138\t   infrastructure).\n139\t\n140\t## Tiered Delivery\n141\t\n142\tNot applicable as a split. The external dependency here is a legal decision,\n143\tnot an upstream delivery with uncertain timing: HLR-1 states the clearance\n144\tblocks **all** shipping work, so no Tier 1 user-facing value can ship ahead of\n145\tthe clearance. Risk-reduction and setup work that can proceed in parallel with\n146\tthe legal review is limited because the candidate itself may change; the\n147\tonboarding chain is therefore fully gated. Partial value exists only across\n148\tthe P0/P1 boundary (operator enablement ships before consumer defaults), which\n149\tis already reflected in the DAG.\n150\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b6e0bf670f5ea51","agent_id":"ac82220c3fa5e34ec","session_id":"73da6f79-aa1d-41ce-bbe1-bfcaf3dba97b","uuid":"367886ad-9a7c-4470-92d4-5187825ae7e3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:52:54.038Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a468b200de8e8a38","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
