{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e522da41f7c85e9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n3\ttitle: Legal clearance for redistributing an AGPL-3.0 S3-compatible object store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Legal clearance for redistributing an AGPL-3.0 S3-compatible object store\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves whether MinIO (AGPL-3.0) can be redistributed as a bundled, supported\n30\tcomponent of the platform — including the derivative-work posture for operator\n31\tintegration — and documents the decision. If the terms cannot be satisfied for\n32\tour distribution model, the investigation confirms the Apache-2.0 fallback\n33\tcandidate (e.g. SeaweedFS) as the replacement upstream and records that image\n34\tproductization work must restart against it. This clearance blocks all\n35\tshipping work in the strategy.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Legal review of redistributing MinIO under AGPL-3.0 in the product's\n40\t  distribution model (including disconnected/install-media redistribution)\n41\t- Determination of the derivative-work posture for integrating the store with\n42\t  the Platform Operator (bundling, deploy, and lifecycle management)\n43\t- A documented clearance decision, including any conditions imposed\n44\t- If clearance is denied: confirmation of the fallback candidate and a\n45\t  statement of the restart impact on image productization\n46\t\n47\t## Questions to Resolve\n48\t\n49\t1. Can MinIO (AGPL-3.0) be redistributed in our distribution model for\n50\t   disconnected installs?\n51\t2. Does Platform Operator integration (bundling, deployment, upgrade\n52\t   management) create a derivative work under AGPL-3.0, and if so, can the\n53\t   posture be made acceptable?\n54\t3. If the terms cannot be satisfied: is the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate\n55\t   (e.g. SeaweedFS) confirmed as the replacement upstream?\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given the legal review of AGPL-3.0 redistribution terms, When the review\n60\t  completes, Then the clearance decision — including the derivative-work\n61\t  posture for operator integration — is documented and accessible to all\n62\t  downstream teams.\n63\t- Measured by: a written clearance decision exists; either redistribution is\n64\t  cleared (possibly with conditions) or the fallback upstream is confirmed\n65\t  with the restart of image productization planned.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): Legal review of redistributing the candidate object store\n70\t  (MinIO, AGPL-3.0) completed and documented, including the derivative-work\n71\t  posture for operator integration.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b6e0bf670f5ea51","agent_id":"ac82220c3fa5e34ec","session_id":"73da6f79-aa1d-41ce-bbe1-bfcaf3dba97b","uuid":"59a84758-d6f3-4f8f-be76-7ac4f62ee26f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:52:59.853Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e522da41f7c85e9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
