tes for the bundled store flow\n52\t  through the operator's upgrade path\n53\t- The bundled store is visible to the platform (inventoried and managed) rather\n54\t  than an invisible field workaround\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Given the productized store image and its midstream repository, When an\n59\t  administrator enables the bundled store through the Platform Operator, Then\n60\t  a supported S3-compatible object store runs on the cluster and is managed\n61\t  through the platform upgrade lifecycle.\n62\t- The store's build pipeline is green (the image is built through the standard\n63\t  Konflux pipeline, not a one-off build).\n64\t- Enabling or not enabling the bundled store does not alter behavior of\n65\t  customer-provided S3 configurations.\n66\t- Measured by: an administrator can enable and use the bundled store on a\n67\t  disconnected cluster without manually installing upstream software.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible\n72\t  object store through the Platform Operator, with productized images and\n73\t  upgrade lifecycle.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b6e0bf670f5ea51","agent_id":"ac82220c3fa5e34ec","session_id":"73da6f79-aa1d-41ce-bbe1-bfcaf3dba97b","uuid":"cd3bd507-7404-4186-bc59-b410edf1bde6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:53:07.161Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8691182340decca8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
