ences a nonexistent epic.\nNo cycles.\n\nImplementation-type parallelism verified pair by pair:\n\n- Rule 7: no license-validation (E003) → repo-onboarding (E002) edge — parallel. Correct.\n- Rule 8: no E003 → E004 (konflux-onboarding) edge. Correct.\n- Rule 10: E004 (konflux-onboarding) checked against **every** general\n  implementation epic — E005, E006, and E007. No edge in either direction. The\n  E004/E005 coupling is correctly enforced via E005's \"build pipeline green\"\n  acceptance criterion (Rule 25), never a DAG edge; the summary states this\n  explicitly. No image-digest/endpoint-URL rationale is used to justify any\n  edge.\n- Rule 9 edge (E003 → E005) is justified and allowed.\n- Rule 11: E008 (docs-authoring) blocked by all six implementation epics. Correct.\n\nCritical path length 5 (E001 → E002 → E005 → E006 → E008) is within the\nM-with-new-component heuristic (4-5) for a 4-HLR, 4-component strategy\nintroducing a new component.\n\nThe direct E001 → E004 and E001 → E005 edges are transitively redundant via\nE002, but are required because gated_by targets must appear in direct\ndependencies — correct, not an issue.\n\nContent scan for uncaptured data dependencies: E005 consumes the productized\nimage (built by E004) but that coupling is the Rule 25 AC by design; E006/E007\nconsume the bundled store capability via E005 edges; E008 consumes\nimplementation results via edges to all implementations. No missing edges.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n\nComponent/team tuples are clean: E002-E005 (Platform Operator / RHOAI Platform\nOperator, split by implementation type per the onboarding chain), E006 (Data\nScience Pipelines / RHOAI Pipelines), E007 (Dashboard / RHOAI Dashboard), E008\n(Documentation / RHOAI Documentation). No epic spans multiple teams.\n\nThe new-component mapping (bundled store has no canonical component entry;\nE002-E005 attributed to Platform Operator as the bundling vehicle) is a\ndocumented, defensible application of the component